{"ref":"2018.MM44.128","summary":"The Premier has announced the government's intent to introduce legislation to reduce the size of City Council to 25 members using the Provincial and Federal ridings. In order to allow City Council to debate the implications of this announcement, City Council should add this matter to the agenda of the current meeting for debate.","decided":"City Council on July 23, 24, 25, 26, 27 and 30, 2018, adopted the following: 1. City Council convey its opposition to the Provincial government's intention to introduce legislation to reduce the size of City Council to 25 Councillors and a Mayor. 2. City Council request the Province of Ontario to conduct a binding referendum on the number and boundaries of wards before proceeding with the legislation. 3. If the Province does not conduct the referendum requested in Part 2 above, City Council urge the Province to amend the Municipal Elections Act or regulations thereunder to permit the City to put a question on the ballot in 2018 on the proposed reduction in the number of wards and Members of Council before the Province proceeds with the legislation. 4. City Council exempt the City Clerk from any established City policies and procedures or any part of an established City policy or procedure related to procurement, human resources, budget and information technology that the City Clerk believes is necessary or desirable in order to conduct the Toronto election. 5. In the event Nomination Day is changed, City Council amend the Constituency Services and Office Budget Policy to add the following: Notwithstanding section 5.1.1 of the Use of City Resources during an Election Period Policy, City Council shift the cut-off date for Councillor communications from August 1, 2018 to August…","motions":[{"stage":"City Council","when":"","desc":"Two-Thirds full Council required - Add urgent motion - Tory","type":"Introduce Motion without Notice","result":"Carried, 34-1","yes":34,"no":1,"votes":[["Ana Bailão","Yes